    "code": "M1",
    "name": "Invitation to attend a MIAM",
    "subject": "An invitation to attend a MIAM, Brighter Future Mediation [{{case_ref}}]",
    "bodyHtml": "<p><br></p><p>Hello {{client_first_name}},</p><p><br></p><p>I hope you are well. I am writing from Brighter Future Mediation because your ex-partner, {{other_party_first_name}}, recently attended a Mediation Information and Assessment Meeting (MIAM) with us. They have expressed their willingness to work together through mediation to reach agreement on {{child_arrangements_financial_matters_both_child_arrangements_and_financial_matte}}.</p><p><br></p><p>Your opportunity to participate</p><p><br></p><p>We would like to invite you to attend your own MIAM, a confidential one-to-one online session lasting up to one hour with an FMC-registered mediator. This is your chance to:</p><p><br></p><p>discuss your situation and concerns in a safe, neutral space</p><p>understand all the options available to you</p><p>learn how mediation could help you reach arrangements that work for your family</p><p>ask questions and make an informed decision about next steps.</p><p><br></p><p>You can find out more about MIAMs and mediation<a href=\"{{link_miam}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_miam}}\">here</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>In most instances a MIAM is a legal requirement before applying to the family court, and it is mandatory to attempt negotiation before court proceedings. There are limited<a href=\"{{link_exemptions}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_exemptions}}\">exemptions</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Why consider mediation?</p><p><br></p><p>You stay in control: decisions are made by you both, not imposed by a judge.</p><p>Faster resolution: reach agreements in weeks, not months or years.</p><p>More affordable: significantly less expensive than solicitors and lengthy court battles.</p><p>Less conflict: focused on cooperation and communication.</p><p>Better for children: research shows mediated agreements lead to better long-term outcomes. We also offer child-inclusive mediation.</p><p>Government support: a £500 voucher is available towards mediation costs when discussing child arrangements.</p><p><br></p><p>What you can expect</p><p><br></p><p>Confidentiality: everything discussed is strictly confidential and cannot be used in court proceedings should mediation not result in agreement.</p><p>Neutrality: the mediator remains neutral and does not advocate for either party.</p><p>Respect: all participants are treated with dignity and respect.</p><p>Self-determination: you keep full control over any decisions and agreements made.</p><p><br></p><p>The government £500 mediation voucher scheme</p><p><br></p><p>We are registered with the MoJ Family Mediation Voucher Scheme that provides up to £500 per case, not per person, towards the cost of mediation sessions.</p><p><br></p><p>It does not cover the MIAM, and it is not a cash payment to you. It is applied directly against your session fees, £250 on your account and £250 on your ex-partner&#x27;s. Standard voucher sessions are covered entirely by the government voucher.</p><p><br></p><p><a href=\"{{link_fees}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_fees}}\">fees page</a>.</p><p>It is available where there is a child under 18 involved in the arrangements being discussed, and where neither of you has claimed before.</p><p>It is not<a href=\"{{link_legalaid}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_legalaid}}\">legal aid</a> and is not means tested. If you think you may qualify for legal aid, you can check your eligibility<a href=\"{{link_legalaid_check}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_legalaid_check}}\">here</a>.</p><p>We apply on your behalf after both of you have attended a MIAM and mediation has been assessed as suitable, so there is nothing for you to do.</p><p>It does not cover missed or late-cancelled sessions.</p><p><br></p><p>We give that first joint session two hours rather than 90 minutes on purpose. It is the session that does the most work. You get through far more in one sitting, you are less likely to need an extra session later to finish the same conversation, and most people reach agreement sooner and spend less overall. MIAMs are available from £125 and full fee information can be found<a href=\"{{link_fees}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_fees}}\">here</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>To book, please reply with your availability over the next two weeks, or call us on 0333 240 8038. If we do not hear from you within 7 days we will assume you do not wish to access mediation at this time, and we will inform your ex-partner that we were unable to book a MIAM.</p><p><br></p><p>We understand this is a difficult time, and we are here to help you navigate it with information and support. You can read more about how mediation compares to court on our<a href=\"{{link_court_blog}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_court_blog}}\">blog</a>, and our<a href=\"{{link_faq}}\"> </a><a href=\"{{link_faq}}\">FAQs</a> answer the questions we are asked most or feel free to give us a call 0333 240 8038.</p><p><br></p><p>.</p>",
