    "bodyHtml": "<p>Hello {{client_first_name}},</p><p><br></p><p>Great news, you have scheduled your MIAM appointment with Jo. We know this can feel like a big step.</p><p><br></p><p>Meeting details</p><p><br></p><p>{{date}} at {{time}} (up to one hour)</p><p><br></p><p>Please join your session using this <a href=\"{{zoom_jo}}\">Zoom meeting link</a></p><p><br></p><p>Meeting ID: 965 6056 1459</p><p><br></p><p>Privacy: your MIAM is an individual, confidential appointment for you to attend without the other party. You must join from a private space where you cannot be overheard or interrupted. No children or other third parties may be present or within hearing distance. Please arrange suitable childcare in advance where necessary, and join showing your first name only.</p><p><br></p><p>Punctuality: please join on time. If you are more than 15 minutes late there may not be enough time to complete the MIAM and it may be recorded as missed. You may then need to book and pay for another appointment.</p><p><br></p><p>Device and internet: please check your connection, camera and microphone before the appointment. You can also view our <a href=\"{{link_zoom_guide}}\">Zoom guide</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Payment</p><p><br></p><p>Fees are payable in advance. Your appointment is confirmed only once payment has been received.</p><p>Payment must reach us at least 72 hours before the appointment, or the held slot is released as per our <a href=\"{{link_terms}}\">terms of use</a>.</p><p>Our current fees are always on our <a href=\"{{link_fees}}\">fees page</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Mediation is:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Voluntary: you make an informed choice about whether to participate.</p><p>2. Impartial: the mediator does not take sides or favour either person.</p><p>3. Confidential: the content of discussions is confidential, subject to limited legal and safeguarding exceptions.</p><p>4. Self-determining: you retain the power to make decisions about your life and circumstances.</p><p><br></p><p>Please do not hesitate to contact us if you have any administrative questions before your appointment.</p><p><br></p><p>If you would like to read ahead, our <a href=\"{{link_faq}}\">FAQs</a> and our guide to <a href=\"{{link_miam_blog}}\">what a MIAM is</a> explain exactly what to expect.</p>",
